So the YouTube video shows 5-6 balls at every frame. This is because:
1. The YouTube video has 15 chains (40 tracklets) that all overlap in time
2. The H10 v5 quality is mostly UNCERTAIN (q ~ 0.4-0.5)
3. Each chain claims to be a different physical ball

This is actually a real problem: the chain representation cannot reliably count balls in a 3-ball cascade because the tracklets are too short to confidently identify a single physical ball. The "4+" inflation is essentially: the model cannot distinguish 3 separate physical balls from 1 ball bouncing 3 times.

Let me check the identity merge candidates more carefully. We found 1 CONFIDENT merge candidate: chain36 -> chain30, -4 frames, right hand, h3=True. Let me investigate:
