Looking at coordinates: at f=890, t62 is at (660, 432) and t63 is at (587, 414). They're 73 pixels apart. So they're at different positions. Maybe these are two different balls that are being juggled simultaneously.

OK so the H11 algorithm's merge candidate is actually a false positive — chain 36 (t62, t66) and chain 30 (t51, 52, 54, 59, 63) are at different positions. They are different physical balls, just both visible at the same time. The vision analyzer was overly confident in the merge.

