- Is sensitive to event density in the window
- The "MIXED_3+" labels mostly reflect "we don't have enough events to classify"
- The "FOUNTAIN_3+" labels are based on same-hand event dominance, but the visual pattern may actually be a cascade

This is a key insight to document. The H12 v2 algorithm is making classification decisions based on the event log, but the event log only contains 8 catch/throw events. The pattern classification is therefore limited by event sparsity.

