Big finding: all 73 identical-video tracklets have exactly 1 arc under v7's sign-change criterion. The zero-crossing detection is too strict — most juggling ball tracks don't have a clean apex because catch-throw motion interrupts the arc. So per-bounce segmentation via sign changes doesn't actually segment anything. The algorithm is essentially using "first arc = whole tracklet" as v5 did, but with shorter K=2 smoothing.

