- h7v2_reclassified mean: 0.201 (n=13) — +0.059 over v4d (90% CI [+0.022, +0.098])
- h7v2_kept_ballistic mean: 0.206 (n=12) — +0.064 over v4d (90% CI [+0.027, +0.102])
- Cohen's d (reclass vs v4d) = +0.965 (LARGE effect)
- Interestingly, h7v2_reclassified is NOT significantly different from h7v2_kept_ballistic on identical (CI includes 0)

YouTube video:
- v4d mean: 0.232 (n=1) — too few to draw conclusions
- h7v2_reclassified mean: 0.303 (n=25) — +0.089 over kept_ballistic (90% CI [+0.070, +0.108])
- h7v2_kept_ballistic mean: 0.214 (n=1) — too few

The key finding: h7v2-reclassified and h7v2-kept-ballistic edges both have higher detector concentration than v4d hand-links. This is because v4d links have longer gaps (18 frames vs 9-10) which means wider search windows, so the n_out_reach denominator is larger. The h7v2 vs h7v2_kept_ballistic difference on identical is small (-0.005) — the detector doesn't strongly distinguish catch+throws from identity switches on identical.

